# 25. Definition of V1

QuantOS V1 is complete when the system can reliably demonstrate the following complete path:

```text
Binance Historical Data
        ↓
Validated Local Dataset
        ↓
Deterministic Features
        ↓
One Production Model
        ↓
Backtest
        ↓
Walk-Forward Validation
        ↓
Monte Carlo / Robustness
        ↓
Paper Trading
        ↓
Risk Approval
        ↓
Binance Spot Execution
        ↓
Trade / Account Recording
        ↓
Evaluation
```

The system must be understandable, reproducible, testable, and safe enough to operate continuously on a local workstation.

---

# 26. Final Rule

QuantOS V1 is intentionally small.

The goal is not to build everything a quantitative trading platform could eventually become.

The goal is to build the smallest complete system that can prove the core idea in real operation.

**Build the foundation. Validate it. Remove unnecessary complexity. Prove robustness. Then expand.**

